18. Implementation Experience and AI Evaluation

The development process demonstrated an important distinction between specification quality and implementation capability.

Claude.ai and Gemini were both given multiple opportunities to produce the map-and-dashboard implementation but were unable to successfully produce the final working result after several attempts.

Claude nevertheless produced several accurate specification conditions that are retained in this document.

ChatGPT ultimately produced the successful Phase 1 map-and-dashboard implementation.

This should not be interpreted as a general ranking of AI systems. It is a record of the actual development experience for this particular component.

The practical lesson for this project is:

«Correct architectural conditions must eventually become working behavior. A specification is successful only when its important conditions can be implemented and tested.»

The specification therefore separates:

1. Required behavior
2. Architectural constraints
3. Implementation decisions
4. Deferred capabilities
5. Observed implementation results

This separation should be maintained as the widget evolves.

